# Core generator roadmap

Work on `backend/app/Core/` (and its immediate callers) in this order. Do not start a later item until the user has reviewed.

**Focus:** Challenge alone stays stable. Future 8+ alone is what we improve. Combined C+F8+ only after F8+ alone is solid.

**Out of scope:** Finale. Explore (side effect — do not break `e_mode` recipes; no Explore work). Matchpläne CRUD (already live). Challenge afternoon/finals and Challenge judging↔RG map. A/B coordinator / shared-stage redesign until item 4. Policy C Future follows stand-alone Future (same `main()`).

Prefer small, behavior-preserving changes. Fix inconsistency only with tests or a clear before/after. When unsure which item a change belongs to, ask before implementing.

## Current architecture

Entry: `PlanGeneratorController` → `PlanGeneratorService` (`isSupported`, `prepare`, `run` / `GeneratePlanJob`) → `PlanGeneratorCore::generate`.

`PlanParameter::load` purges off-event overrides, syncs Challenge-shaped modes from team counts, then loads joint + attached program catalog rows. `ProgramPresence` resolves attached / on programs. **Ceremony lead** = lowest `m_first_program.sequence` among Challenge-shaped programs that are on (`leadProgramId`). `$this->lead = $this->challenge ?? $this->future`. When both are on, **both generate** — do not restore skip-generate (`skippedLeadProgramIds()` is leftover naming).

If `g_finale` → `FinaleGenerator` (Day 2 via `generateOneDayEvent`, then custom Day 1). **Do not work on Finale.** Else `generateOneDayEvent`: build `ChallengeGenerator` and/or `Future8Generator` (`ChallengeShapedLead`); Core `e_mode` recipes (`runLeadRecipes`) drive the **lead** (Challenge if on, else Future). `e_mode` 6/7 stay reserved.

`runMain`: one program → `lead->main()`; both on + `g_separate_rooms` → Policy C (Challenge `main()`, then Future `main()` from the same opening end); else `GameRoundCoordinator` Policy A (`g_per_round`) or B (`PolicyBRoundScheduler`). A/B morning is hardcoded game rounds 0–3. Joint ceremony prefix: `c+f8_*` when Explore is off; `g_*` when Explore is integrated.

Clocks: each Challenge-shaped generator owns `cTime` / `jTime` / `rTime`. Core owns Explore `eTime`. Coupling: `IntegratedExploreState` (datetime `rg1End` / `startTime`). Writer: `ActivityWriter` → `activity_group` + `activity`. Afternoon: Core walks `AfternoonBlockOrderService`. After generate: `FreeBlockGenerator`, then `SlotBlockPlanSyncService`.

Pauses after TR/RG/finals are **duration-only** (`addMinutes`). Free + slot extra-blocks only. Judging and games stay in **one loop**.

Match lists today: both programs use `MatchPlanSpec::for` → `MatchPlanBuilder` (rounds 0–3) into live `match` (`plan` + `first_program`). Catalog `m_match` CRUD is live; **generate does not read it**.

Nothing currently calls `PlanGeneratorCore::generate` in tests.

## Challenge vs Future 8+ (today)

Same shape: `ChallengeShapedLead` (opening → `main` judging ∥ games → afternoon pieces → awards). Same constructor formulas, same Challenge compress map on Future, same `RobotGameGenerator` write loop.

Challenge-only: `c_` / `j_` / `r_`; robot check (`r_robot_check`, `r_check`, `r_duration_robot_check`); `c_lunch_break_early`; hard lunch activity; finale Day 2 map; afternoon presentations + `r_final_16|8|4|2`.

Future-only today: `f8_*` (`f8_fields` = tables); `RobotGameWriteConfig::future8()` `checkCode: null`; no early-lunch param; hard lunch advances clocks only; afternoon `f8_presentations` plus leftover empty extra rounds (see item 3.4).

Dual: Policy C = parallel solos. A/B = coordinator. Test round always parallel. Policy C Future uses `setCoordinateExplore(false)`.

Do not merge the two generator classes until Challenge is locked and F8+ alone is solid (optional item 5).

